00:50:53,083 --> 00:50:56,333
And where, may we ask,
is, uh, Mr. Moretti?

956
00:50:57,416 --> 00:51:00,124
You know, Eddie, he's not gonna make it.

957
00:51:00,125 --> 00:51:02,665
- Just like my girlfriend, he's also busy.
- Ah.

958
00:51:02,666 --> 00:51:05,249
Wasn't the most straightforward
of operations.

959
00:51:05,250 --> 00:51:06,915
There's the fruits of our labor.

960
00:51:06,916 --> 00:51:09,958
It's going to be money well spent,
trust me. Marco's gonna love it.

961
00:51:10,708 --> 00:51:13,125
Only last night he told me
how much he loves that Botticelli.

962
00:51:13,791 --> 00:51:16,708
He'd heard about the sale
and regrets he didn't buy it.

963
00:51:17,458 --> 00:51:21,165
Good. Just a shame
that he can't be here himself.

964
00:51:21,166 --> 00:51:22,000
I know.

965
00:51:22,500 --> 00:51:25,208
But, um, Eddie, my friend, look.

966
00:51:25,958 --> 00:51:29,790
If you want,
you can always leave the picture here.

967
00:51:29,791 --> 00:51:31,457
I'll make sure he gets your elegant gift.

968
00:51:31,458 --> 00:51:33,582
I think we'd rather
give it to Marco ourselves.

969
00:51:33,583 --> 00:51:35,208
Since we've paid so much.

970
00:51:36,083 --> 00:51:38,000
Well, he's a busy man.

971
00:51:38,541 --> 00:51:42,249
You know, I know how to use
the right words with him.

972
00:51:42,250 --> 00:51:44,540
Choose the right moment.

973
00:51:44,541 --> 00:51:47,666
And his legs will open
like the parting of the Red Sea.

974
00:51:50,041 --> 00:51:52,874
You never invited him here
in the first place, did you, Cico?

975
00:51:52,875 --> 00:51:56,041
Or do you prefer
to be called Gino de Bambi?

976
00:52:02,291 --> 00:52:05,582
I, uh… I… I'm so sorry, but is there
a problem here or something?

977
00:52:05,583 --> 00:52:07,458
Yes, there is a problem.

978
00:52:08,375 --> 00:52:09,874
[Susie] We know the picture's yours.

979
00:52:09,875 --> 00:52:12,582
We know the price
was artificially inflated on your side.

980
00:52:12,583 --> 00:52:15,374
And that you hired kids
to try and nick it once we'd bought it

981
00:52:15,375 --> 00:52:18,165
so we'd never get the chance
to give it to Marco ourselves.

982
00:52:18,166 --> 00:52:22,624
Fortunately, your subcontractors ended up
being as unreliable as you are.

983
00:52:22,625 --> 00:52:26,582
[Eddie] They did that because
the entire enterprise is invention.

984
00:52:26,583 --> 00:52:31,249
So, where would you like to go
from here, Cico?

985
00:52:31,250 --> 00:52:32,665
[chuckles awkwardly]

986
00:52:32,666 --> 00:52:34,083
[tense music plays]

987
00:52:35,500 --> 00:52:36,375
[Cico] Okay.

988
00:52:41,875 --> 00:52:44,915
You think you can tell me what to do?

989
00:52:44,916 --> 00:52:46,750
A couple of salad sellers?

990
00:52:47,458 --> 00:52:48,790
You wanna take me on?

991
00:52:48,791 --> 00:52:50,791
You wanna take the fucking Mafia on?

992
00:52:51,791 --> 00:52:55,374
Why don't we ask Marco
what exactly you do for the Mafia?

993
00:52:55,375 --> 00:52:57,583
And how are we going to do that, Eddie?

994
00:52:58,875 --> 00:53:01,374
Well, we're gonna ask him ourselves.

995
00:53:01,375 --> 00:53:03,957
I think that's him right now, isn't it?

996
00:53:03,958 --> 00:53:05,416
- Believe so.
- [Eddie] Mm.

997
00:53:07,250 --> 00:53:11,790
You see, because you didn't call him,
we did. And we brought him up to speed.

998
00:53:11,791 --> 00:53:15,416
[Susie] And you're right.
He's very excited about the painting.

999
00:53:16,541 --> 00:53:18,165
First he'd heard of it, apparently.

1000
00:53:18,166 --> 00:53:20,166
[tense music builds]

1001
00:53:21,708 --> 00:53:22,665
Fuck.

1002
00:53:22,666 --> 00:53:24,124
[Marco speaks Italian]

1003
00:53:24,125 --> 00:53:25,500
{\an8}[Cico in Italian]

1004
00:53:27,750 --> 00:53:32,708
- [music fades]
- [Marco speaks Italian]

1005
00:53:35,208 --> 00:53:39,749
[in English] Quiet. Be quiet now.
Uh, the grown-ups are talking now.

1006
00:53:39,750 --> 00:53:40,875
{\an8}[in Italian]

1007
00:53:42,791 --> 00:53:44,165
{\an8}[Cico]

1008
00:53:44,166 --> 00:53:45,458
[shouts in Italian]

1009
00:53:48,541 --> 00:53:51,332
[in English] Eddie, nice to meet you.
Thank you for your call.

1010
00:53:51,333 --> 00:53:53,374
I'm sorry we are meeting like this.

1011
00:53:53,375 --> 00:53:57,790
How should we resolve this situation?

1012
00:53:57,791 --> 00:53:58,958
Mr. Moretti,

1013
00:53:59,625 --> 00:54:01,915
this is your country, your rules.

1014
00:54:01,916 --> 00:54:06,249
And I'm confident that you are best placed
to decide the appropriate outcome.

1015
00:54:06,250 --> 00:54:07,541
{\an8}[in Italian]

1016
00:54:08,541 --> 00:54:10,749
[in English] But in my experience, uh,

1017
00:54:10,750 --> 00:54:15,000
kindness is always mistaken for weakness.

1018
00:54:17,458 --> 00:54:20,041
Cico, you are a snake.

1019
00:54:20,625 --> 00:54:23,416
Pretty to look at. Dirty to touch.

1020
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:27,250
It hurts me
because it will hurt my goddaughter.

1021
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:31,041
And I think you don't know
where is your place in the food chain.

1022
00:54:31,958 --> 00:54:32,833
So,

1023
00:54:34,125 --> 00:54:35,375
I will show you.

1024
00:54:36,416 --> 00:54:38,250
[tiger growls]

1025
00:54:41,750 --> 00:54:43,958
[tiger roars]

1026
00:54:44,958 --> 00:54:47,540
[panicked breathing]

1027
00:54:47,541 --> 00:54:49,583
[growls]

1028
00:54:51,666 --> 00:54:52,916
{\an8}[man in Italian]

1029
00:54:53,666 --> 00:54:55,082
{\an8}[Marco]

1030
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:56,124
[muffled screaming]

1031
00:54:56,125 --> 00:54:58,583
[in English] Cico was always a…
a messy guy.

1032
00:54:59,625 --> 00:55:01,541
Maybe this is the fitting end for him.

1033
00:55:02,041 --> 00:55:06,165
So moving forward,
we could, uh, come to an understanding.

1034
00:55:06,166 --> 00:55:08,874
- You appreciate that, don't you?
- Of course.

1035
00:55:08,875 --> 00:55:11,332
[Marco] This operation you have set up

1036
00:55:11,333 --> 00:55:16,832
within the grounds
of my goddaughter's estate, eh,

1037
00:55:16,833 --> 00:55:19,540
if I well understand,
there are others like it?

1038
00:55:19,541 --> 00:55:21,207
Well, as it happens,

1039
00:55:21,208 --> 00:55:24,749
we are keen to set up
further operations in the south,

1040
00:55:24,750 --> 00:55:30,249
in the fullness of time,
with someone that we, uh, could rely upon.

1041
00:55:30,250 --> 00:55:33,499
Oof. We could help a lot in the south.

1042
00:55:33,500 --> 00:55:35,915
- [cage rattles]
- [muffled shouting]

1043
00:55:35,916 --> 00:55:38,708
How about five million a month
for your protection and support?

1044
00:55:39,625 --> 00:55:40,915
[muffled shouting]

1045
00:55:40,916 --> 00:55:41,916
[tiger growls]

1046
00:55:42,666 --> 00:55:44,083
[poignant music plays]

1047
00:55:47,750 --> 00:55:49,416
- Thank you.
- [Cico yells]

1048
00:55:58,083 --> 00:55:59,125
Enzo!

1049
00:55:59,875 --> 00:56:01,207
{\an8}[in Italian]

1050
00:56:01,208 --> 00:56:03,083
[roars]

1051
00:56:04,625 --> 00:56:06,083
[muffled straining]

1052
00:56:07,125 --> 00:56:08,208
[in English] Fifteen.

1053
00:56:09,458 --> 00:56:11,000
[muffled screaming]

1054
00:56:15,416 --> 00:56:16,458
Seven and a half.

1055
00:56:20,583 --> 00:56:21,416
Ten.

1056
00:56:24,500 --> 00:56:27,457
Can he be trusted?

1057
00:56:27,458 --> 00:56:29,666
- [tiger growls]
- [muffled screaming]

1058
00:56:30,833 --> 00:56:32,207
{\an8}[in Italian]

1059
00:56:32,208 --> 00:56:35,041
{\an8}[Cico yells]

1060
00:56:35,916 --> 00:56:37,624
[dramatic operatic music plays]

1061
00:56:37,625 --> 00:56:39,582
[roars]

1062
00:56:39,583 --> 00:56:41,375
[panicked shouting]

1063
00:56:44,625 --> 00:56:46,291
[muffled screaming]

1064
00:56:49,250 --> 00:56:51,290
[in English] I look forward
to doing business.

1065
00:56:51,291 --> 00:56:53,666
Can the Duke be trusted?

1066
00:56:54,583 --> 00:56:56,041
[muffled screaming]

1067
00:56:56,708 --> 00:56:57,624
{\an8}[in Italian]

1068
00:56:57,625 --> 00:56:59,625
[muffled screaming]

1069
00:57:05,333 --> 00:57:07,083
[muffled shouting]

1070
00:57:15,125 --> 00:57:16,165
Enzo!

1071
00:57:16,166 --> 00:57:17,250
{\an8}[in Italian]

1072
00:57:17,916 --> 00:57:19,749
{\an8}[muffled screaming]

1073
00:57:19,750 --> 00:57:21,040
[tiger growls]

1074
00:57:21,041 --> 00:57:23,375
[Cico breathes shakily]

1075
00:57:27,750 --> 00:57:29,416
[tiger snarls]

1076
00:57:38,125 --> 00:57:39,083
[in English] Right.

1077
00:59:59,416 --> 01:00:00,583
[music fades]

